      {
        "id": 242208,
        "name": "FrivYeti",
        "username": "FrivYeti",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/frivyeti/{size}/1919_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-01-20T16:51:08.079Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I would have read the card the same way as you, but this is how the game tends to read it. Whispers of Oblivion hits each target one at a time. As soon as hitting a target destroys it, the healing effect triggers and heals all the Manifestations.</p>\n<p>If you’re up against Heroic Infinitor, him placing Manifestations under himself doesn’t count as destroying them, so what probably happened was that it hit and destroyed a hero target and healed all the Manifestations. You can avoid that by controlling the order in which Infinitor hits things.</p>\n<p>If it healed everything before hitting anything, that’s a bug and should be reported.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2022-01-20T16:51:08.079Z",
        "reply_count": 1,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 32,
